099", "personaname": "Oberfeldwebel", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198141835099/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 8, "playtime_forever": 150260, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 929, "playtime_at_review": 8015, "last_played": 1791058332, "avatar": "19b0eb02d1c9c1ddefb465f58857d35d6f5b82e0"}, "language": "english", "review": "Disclaimer: if you decided to get this game because you saw Funny clips from the bigger Youtubers Watch an entire OP, as most units dont have 100% of the operation being you just meming around mostly it is just driving,Walking or flying and not actual Combat (i made that mistake)   \n\nThe Game is beautifull especially with the right Unit and people, The Search for a unit can be difficult and sometimes not even be what you imagined or what was advertised but when have one the Game will essentially become infinitly replayable, it is Super modable and extremly Diverse in the Way that you play it, either as a more arcady shooter or Full blown Real life Simulation\n\nThe graphics and sound design hold up decently for how old the game is and allow for a \"immersive\" Game experience\n\nHowever not all games are without flaw this game has Physics issues meaning sometimes if you crash your T14 into a Pebble it might attempt to reenact the Apollo 15 mission or the AI might switch form being the Terminator to essentially Braindead, nothing is Completly Certain only that SOMETHING will go wrong either command being Flung into Space, your Game crashes, a physics object get's flung around and knock's you out for no reason or you get shot from 2 Continents away, \n\nConclusion: a Good Game with sometimes Hilarious bugs (Inevitable nowadays tbh) with a good variety in what you can do, it is However HEAVILY reliant in what community you join Recommended 9/10", "timestamp_created": 1596842028, "timestamp_updated": 1596842028, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "